    "summary": "Acoustic opener, Mason's Children debut, high‑energy second set",
    "blurb": "The show opens with a spontaneous acoustic mini‑set before launching into a fiery electric half. Highlights include Black Peter, Hard To Handle, The Other One jam and the first performance of Mason's Children. Recording quality is solid throughout, making it a great snapshot of late‑1969 Dead.",
    "review": "December 19, 1969 at the Fillmore finds the Dead in top form, kicking off with an impromptu acoustic duo as Phil battles traffic. Jerry’s clean, resonant guitar and Bob’s steady rhythm set a relaxed tone before the band erupts into a high‑octane second set. Standout moments include a gritty Black Peter that showcases Phil’s deepening bass groove, a scorching Hard To Handle where the twins lock in tight, and an adventurous The Other One that rolls seamlessly through the double Cryptical Envelopment tease. The debut of Mason's Children adds a fresh, upbeat flavor to the mix, while Good Lovin' and Turn On Your Lovelight close the night on a joyous note. All three soundboard sources capture the energy clearly, but the Clugston recording preserves the acoustic opener’s intimacy alongside the electric fire with exceptional clarity.",
